# Method Parameter Typing

## Functions with 3+ Parameters

When a function or method has 3 or more parameters, use a type for better maintainability and type safety.

**Avoid:**

```typescript
function processData(param1: string, param2: number, param3: boolean, param4: string) {
  // implementation
}
```

**Prefer:**

```typescript
type ProcessDataArgs = {
  param1: string;
  param2: number;
  param3: boolean;
  param4: string;
};

function processData(args: ProcessDataArgs) {
  // implementation
}
```

## Auto-Suggestion Rule

When you see a function with 3 or more parameters, suggest refactoring to use a type for the parameters.
